# THE NEGATIVE CONTROL for the missing-library guard, and it is the row that
# makes the guard a guard rather than a blanket refusal.
#
# `nolib.h` names a library that cannot exist. Importing it and never touching
# its functions emits no DT_NEEDED at all, so this is a working program and must
# stay one -- diagnosing it would be a guard firing on a program that does not
# have the defect. A #define costs no import, so the marker still proves the
# header was really read.
import "nolib.h"
print("imported")
print(NOLIB_MARKER)
